%N A400577 a(0) = 1; a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n-1} binomial(n-1,k) * k! * a(k).
%F A400577 E.g.f. A(x) satisfies: A'(x) = exp(x) * B(x), A(0)=1, where B(x) = Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*x^n is the o.g.f.
%F A400577 a(n) ~ c * A000178(n-1) = c * BarnesG(n+2) / n!, where c = 5.78838982568354070616737064508388211529002943988753235221127999920534267508967... - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Sep 30 2026
%t A400577 a[0] = 1; a[n_] := a[n] = Sum[Binomial[n - 1, k] k! a[k], {k, 0, n - 1}]; Table[a[n], {n, 0, 14}]
